.TH XAOS 6 "October 2026" "XaoS 3.6" "Helios Games"
.SH NAME
xaos \- interactive fractal explorer with distributed Helios rendering
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xaos
.RB [ \-size " widthxheight"]
.RB [ \-display " display"]
.RB [ \-processors " all|count"]
.SH DESCRIPTION
XaoS displays and animates Mandelbrot, Julia and other fractals using X11.
Hold the left mouse button to zoom in, the right button to zoom out,
and the middle button to move the view.
Use the menu bar for formulas, colours, filters, tutorials and help.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-processors " all|count"
Select the number of render processors, including the caller.
The default is
.BR all .
Available T800/T805 processors are obtained through the session's
Taskforce Manager. The system processor is excluded.
The window title shows the live count.
A count of 1 selects the original serial renderer.
.TP
.BI \-size " widthxheight"
Set the initial window size, for example 640x480.
Smaller images require less calculation and link traffic.
.TP
.BI \-display " display"
Select an X server instead of DISPLAY.
.TP
.B \-helios-profile
Report calculation and synchronized X11 transfer timings on standard error.
.TP
.B \-help
List the available XaoS options.
.SH PROCESSORS
Worker tasks have separate memory and exchange jobs through native Helios
channels. The coordinator preserves XaoS's incremental zoom cache.
Distributed workers calculate missing pixels exactly; the serial renderer
can also use boundary tracing and solid guessing.
.PP
Interactive zooming uses the original adaptive preview renderer in both axes.
Once movement and zoom coasting stop, the workers finish the missing pixels
without the preview time limit. Input is still processed; a new mouse gesture
or resize can interrupt that final pass.
.PP
Worker reservations last until XaoS exits.
Obtaining every spare processor may prevent a new login from obtaining one.
Use a smaller count when additional sessions need to start.
An unresponsive worker is dropped after a 30-second job timeout and its
pending work is calculated locally.
.SH PERFORMANCE
Every displayed frame is sent to the X server.
A 640x480 image at 32 bits per pixel contains 1,228,800 bytes.
More render processors do not reduce this display traffic.
.PP
Two full-size pixel buffers remain on the calling processor.
Workers do not pool their RAM.
If a resize cannot allocate these buffers, the previous window size is restored.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/xaos.cfg
User configuration, saved through the XaoS menus.
.TP
.B /helios/local/share/xaos
Tutorials, examples, help and catalogue files.
.SH LIMITATIONS
PNG export and the optional custom-formula parser are not included.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR X (1)
